If any accounting option is chosen at loan product level then:

Debit: Loans Receivable

Credit: Over Payments

Reversal/Adjustment is required (using existing api loans/\{loanId}/transactions/\{transactionId})

 

*Main Rules*

The loan must be in Overpaid status and the refund Amount must be >0 and <= the loan total_overpaid_derived amount

If the refund is partial the loan will remain in Overpaid status and the loan total_overpaid_derived reduced accordingly.

For a full refund (amount = loan total_overpaid_derived) the loan status will be changed to Closed Obligation Met.

 

*Other Rules*

The intention is to record the refund transaction with the least validation possible.  Holiday/Working Days restrictions are not considered.  Nor is the active/inactive status of the client/group.

However, the Refund Date being After the Last Repayment is enforced.

 

