select client_id, constitution_cv_id, main_business_line_cv_id, incorp_no from m_client_non_person;
 1 | 23 | 24 | INC-001
{code}

Expected result: the response includes clientNonPersonDetails (constitution, mainBusinessLine, incorpNumber, incorpValidityTillDate, remarks), as the client data already supports.

Cause:
ClientReadPlatformServiceImpl.retrieveOne() builds the response with ClientMapper.map(client), and ClientMapper has

{code}
@Mapping(target = "clientNonPersonDetails", ignore = true)
{code}

(fineract-provider/src/main/java/org/apache/fineract/portfolio/client/mapper/ClientMapper.java). Nothing else in retrieveOne() sets the field, so it is always null. The SQL row mapper used elsewhere in ClientReadPlatformServiceImpl still builds ClientNonPersonData. The single-client path seems to have lost it when ClientMapper was added (FINERACT-1760).

