Since the meeting commands moved to the new command processing (FINERACT-2548), POST /centers/\{centerId}/meetings rejects every attendance entry, even for clients who are in the center. Missing or incomplete clientsAttendance also gives a 500 instead of a validation error.

*Steps to reproduce* (center 5 has group 6, client 7 is an active member of group 6, the center has a weekly Tuesday calendar 6 starting 01 September 2026):

{code:json}
POST /fineract-provider/api/v1/centers/5/meetings
{
  "calendarId": 6, "meetingDate": "06 October 2026",
  "dateFormat": "dd MMMM yyyy", "locale": "en",
  "clientsAttendance": [ { "clientId": 7, "attendanceType": { "id": 1 } } ]
}
{code}

*Actual result:* HTTP 403, "Client with identifier null is not in center 5" (error.msg.client.not.in.center).
*Expected result:* the meeting and the attendance are saved.

*Cause* (MeetingWriteServiceImpl.getClientsAttendance, fineract-provider/.../portfolio/meeting/service/MeetingWriteServiceImpl.java):

{code:java}
.filter(group -> group.isChildClient(attendance.getId())).count();
{code}

{{attendance.getId()}} is the id of the attendance record, which is always null when creating a meeting. It should be {{attendance.getClientId()}}. The code before FINERACT-2548 (MeetingWritePlatformServiceJpaRepositoryImpl) used the client id: {{group.isChildClient(clientId)}}. The group branch and the center error message use {{attendance.getId()}} too, so the group error says "Client with identifier null is not in group" as well.

*Related problems in the same method:*

# No clientsAttendance in the request:
{code:json}
POST /fineract-provider/api/v1/groups/2/meetings
{ "calendarId": 2, "meetingDate": "05 October 2026", "dateFormat": "dd MMMM yyyy", "locale": "en" }
{code}
Actual: HTTP 500 ({{for (var attendance : attendances)}} with attendances == null). The field is not @NotNull, so either it is optional and null should mean no attendance, or it should be rejected with a 400.
# An attendance entry without clientId gives HTTP 500. MeetingAttendanceData has @NotNull on clientId and attendanceType, but the list in MeetingCreateRequest is not annotated @Valid, so those constraints are never checked. Request body part:
{code:json}
"clientsAttendance": [ { "attendanceType": { "id": 1 } } ]
{code}

For comparison, a valid group meeting on group 2 returns 200, so the group path works when the data is complete:
{code:json}
"clientsAttendance": [ { "clientId": 5, "attendanceType": { "id": 1 } } ]
{code}

*Question:* before the new command processing, attendanceType was a number. It now has to be an object with an id; a number gives 400 "The referenced JSON data is invalid". The Mifos web app still sends a number. Was this change intended? If yes, the web app needs an update; if not, the API could accept both.
{code:json}
"attendanceType": 1            (old format, now 400)
"attendanceType": { "id": 1 }  (new format)
{code}

*Possible fix:* use {{attendance.getClientId()}} in the group and center checks, treat a null clientsAttendance as an empty list (or validate it), add @Valid to the list, and add integration tests for center attendance and the validation cases.

